00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.980
Quantum computing funding from the Chips Act creates a fresh satellite entry point for tech

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:48.740
exposure in registered accounts. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,501, up 1.1%. The NASDAQ closed at 26,518,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:59.360
up 1.9%. The TSX composite finished flat at 34,969. European equities are positioned to

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.880
lead the second half as peace prospects ease stagflation risks. South Korean chip sector bonuses

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:11.520
are flagging potential inflation spillovers that could influence Bank of Canada and fed timing.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:18.480
Bitcoin rebounded above $63,000, with regulatory developments now the dominant driver

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:25.320
for crypto allocations. Portfolio benchmark data versus the NASDAQ is unavailable in today's feed,

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:31.040
so we will skip alpha commentary. With those broad market moves setting the stage,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:36.440
let us look at how to actually capture the pockets the indexes miss. Core satellite

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:44.260
construction lets investors anchor most of a TFSA or RRSP in low cost broad market ETS.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:50.680
A smaller sleeve then targets time-bound opportunities that broad indexes will not fully capture.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.920
Today's Chips Act, quantum funding and European growth outlook make the satellite sleeve

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:06.580
especially relevant. Build the core with XEQT or VTI slash VXUS at 70 to 80% of the portfolio.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:14.160
Allocate 20 to 30% to single name or sector satellites, such as quantum or European cyclicals.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.340
Rebalance the satellite sleeve quarterly or when any position doubles in weight.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.420
Sell the satellite once the catalyst has been fully priced in or the thesis breaks.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:29.880
The approach has historically delivered excess returns during policy driven rotations

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.540
while keeping overall costs and tax drag low in registered accounts.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:40.760
The main risk is over-concentration in the satellite if multiple catalysts arrive at once.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:46.080
That framework is exactly why we are watching one specific quantum name this week.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:52.420
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. Today's practice investment is

00:02:52.420 --> 00:03:00.520
Regetti Computing ticker RGTI on the NASDAQ. The catalyst is a $100 million federal allocation

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.380
from the Chips Act, earmarked for quantum computing research.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.820
The technical setup has no 20-day volume or moving average data available,

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:15.040
so we size the position assuming standard liquidity for a small cap tech name.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:21.840
Risk assessment shows quantum names can retrace 15 to 20% on any delay in funding milestones.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:30.280
We set a mental stop at 12% below entry. The target is plus 4% to plus 8% over the

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:37.100
five-day window if sector rotation into quantum continues. Confidence is medium because we have

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:44.320
a single clear policy catalyst with no confirming volume data yet. This trade isolates a pure policy

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:50.940
driven catalyst in a sector with positive historical alpha while forcing explicit position sizing and

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:57.540
stop discipline before entry. Listeners learn to quantify how much of the move is already priced

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:03.240
versus still ahead. Before we check how last week's trade performed, remember the rule we learned

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:11.200
the hard way. Last week's simulated hold was ION. Market data was unavailable for evaluation so we

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.060
could not measure whether the leadership change catalyst produced any excess return relative to

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:25.640
the broader market. The running total stands at $396.68. The win rate is 20 wins out of 38 total

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:32.500
trades or 53%. The lesson learned is that without closing prices we cannot measure whether the

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:37.400
leadership change catalyst produced any excess return relative to the broader market.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:43.660
The rule is to require closing price confirmation before declaring any catalyst trade complete.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.000
With that discipline in mind, here are two platform tools that help enforce it.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:56.160
Well-simple trade options chain now surfaces 30-day covered call yields directly on the position

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:04.140
screen for any Canadian or US equity. This gives TFSA holders an immediate view of income they could

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:10.520
generate without leaving the platform. Intermediate investors who already hold individual names should

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:16.680
enable the feature and run a 15-minute scan of their top five holdings to see annualized yields.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:23.600
The interactive brokers TWS scanner lets users filter for stocks with both a fundamental catalyst

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:31.080
such as earnings, revision, or funding announcement, and volume at least 150% of the 20-day average.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:37.340
Canadian users can run the scan in pre-market to surface names that meet the dual catalyst rule

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:43.300
before the open. While you are scanning, keep an eye on these three quick developments. Bitcoin

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:52.020
rebounded above $63,000 according to investing.com. Regulatory clarity is now the primary driver for

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:58.560
crypto allocations rather than macro sentiment. Traders are assessing regulatory developments as the

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:04.940
dominant factor behind the move. The rebound shows allocations responding directly to policy signals

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:12.860
instead of broader economic trends. Investors are directed to add 1-2% Bitcoin exposure via

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:21.240
a CAD-listed ETF. Exposure applies only if the price holds above $63,000 on daily close.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.540
This approach isolates regulatory catalysts while limiting allocation size.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:34.220
Marvell technology saw Nvidia's CEO comment on a potential $1 trillion market cap for the company

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:42.620
Perfool.com. The comment highlights how AI infrastructure spending can lift adjacent semiconductor names.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:50.280
Valuation debate now centers on whether Marvell can reach that scale through its own AI-related products.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:56.740
The discussion positions Marvell as a beneficiary of continued capital expenditure in data centers.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:03.040
Investors are advised to add MRVL to the tech satellite watch list. Any entry

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.500
weights for a pullback to the 50-day moving average. This sequencing separates commentary-driven

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:15.320
interest from actual price confirmation. Space X stock has already climbed double digits since listing

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:22.880
according to Fool.com. The post IPO price action demonstrates how quickly new issues can price in growth

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:29.500
expectations. Rapid gains reflect immediate incorporation of expansion plans into the share price.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:35.360
Market participants are observing whether momentum sustains through the initial trading period.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:42.280
Investors are told to hold off on new space X exposure. The weight extends until the next earnings

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:49.080
window or a 10% retrace occurs. This timing rule prevents entry after the initial re-rating has

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:58.940
already taken place. Our simulated portfolio running total stands at $396.68 with a 53% win rate across

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:06.040
38 trades. Alpha versus the NASDAQ could not be calculated because market data for the period remains

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:12.720
unavailable. The AI analysis is learning from catalyst confirmation patterns and adjusting future

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:19.440
position sizing accordingly. Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong and it cost me

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:26.560
money before I figured it out. Imagine you added a 15% satellite position in a quantum computing name

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:32.800
last week after the chips act announcement. Your order filled at the opening print but the actual

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:40.420
execution reflected a 0.8% premium to the previous close because the stock's average daily volume is

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:49.580
under 2 million shares. The mechanism is simple. The core, such as XEQT or VTI, trades with sub penny

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:57.780
spreads and massive depth. The satellite can gap 1-2% on modest news flow so the 15% sleeve can swing

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:04.400
the entire portfolio by 20-30 basis points on any given day. Professionals always check the 20-day

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:10.000
average dollar volume and the bid ask spread in the first 15 minutes before sizing the satellite.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:16.340
Most retail investors skip this step and end up paying the spread twice once on entry and again

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:22.340
on the quarterly rebalance. The biggest mistake with core satellite is letting a satellite position

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:30.640
grow past 25% of the total account without trimming. Instead set a hard 20% cap and rebalance back to

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:38.140
target every 90 days or on a 50% gain whichever comes first. Pull up any tech name in your TFSA,

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:44.580
calculate the 30-day covered call yield on the nearest out of the money strike and note the annualized

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:50.540
figure. That is the income you are currently leaving on the table. Before we wrap, watch for any

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:56.740
